<!-- ================= FAQ ================= -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="col">
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="rise">Before you order</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>How high is it, exactly?</summary>
        <div class="a"><p>25cm. A dining chair is around 45cm. Sitting on your own heels is around 19cm — so the stool puts you roughly six centimetres above where you'd otherwise be sitting.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I make sujud on the stool?</summary>
        <div class="a"><p>No. You come off the seat and your forehead goes to the floor, exactly as it always has. There is no shelf and nothing goes under your head.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Where does it go in the row?</summary>
        <div class="a"><p>Underneath you. You stand over it, so it never sits behind you obstructing the person praying there, and you never have to fetch it from the back or move it mid-prayer.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Will it slide or rock on a prayer mat?</summary>
        <div class="a"><p>The frame is a continuous curved runner rather than four separate legs, so the load spreads along the mat instead of concentrating in four points.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is it appropriate for my madhhab?</summary>
